{"id":"http.cookies/Morsel","module":"http.cookies","qualname":"Morsel","name":"Morsel","kind":"class","parent":null,"signatures":[],"doc":"A class to hold ONE (key, value) pair.\n\nIn a cookie, each such pair may have several attributes, so this class is\nused to keep the attributes associated with the appropriate key,value pair.\nThis class also includes a coded_value attribute, which is used to hold\nthe network representation of the value.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/http.cookies.html#http.cookies.Morsel","added":null,"changed":[{"version":"3.5","text":"__eq__() now takes key and value into account."},{"version":"3.7","text":"Attributes key, value and coded_value are read-only. Use set() for setting them."},{"version":"3.8","text":"Added support for the samesite attribute."},{"version":"3.14","text":"Added support for the partitioned attribute."}],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/http/cookies.py","line":246},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
